oaded a brand new my  hero academia video where we explain all  the known pro heroes in the show so be  sure to check that out link in the  description and the next episode is set  to focus on the League of villains and  shigaraki so I'm really looking forward  to that  misty connects ER released a short  teaser this week for the second episode  of his independent animation project  Krone Exia and the eight seals now even  though this was only a short teaser you  could tell right away that the quality  of the animation was way better than the  first episode which I was really happy  to see and after the video mists he  actually said that he's been looking at  all the feedback they've been receiving  about the first episode and they've been  actively working on improving the show  for the next episode now personally I  definitely respect misty for doing this  he could have easily said hey I'm a  successful youtuber I don't need to  listen to anybody I'm going to do what I  want or he could have said I'm a  successful youtuber I'm going to do what  works on my channel I'm going to abandon  this project it's way too time-consuming  but instead he said he is listening to  the feedback he is doing his best to  improve the project based on the  constructive feedback he received and I  think he needs to be commended for that  if you want to check out the teaser and  see for yourself the link is in the  description  Aki teareth released a video this week  about anime that are hugely popular in  Japan but never really caught on in most  Western countries and I thought that  this was a really interesting video I  also really appreciated her epic  pronunciation of Doraemon I'm glad that  I've been able to catch up on some of  Aki's videos lately because she has been  spending a lot of time in Japan and so  she's been making content telling anime  fans outside of Japan what Japan is  really like and I think that this is  really important for us anime fans to  know because anime